SUMMARY: Frequency: Shel Khan
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Frequency — a monthly live music series at Worth 
 Gallery. Frequency spotlights BIPOC musicians of varying genres through i
 ntimate\, stripped-back shows. Celebrating sound\, connection\, and creat
 ive expression in Toronto's vibrant music scene. Find your new favorite m
 usician in your new favorite gallery. This month's edition of Frequency f
 eatures Shel Khan\, an existential genre bending musician exploring diffe
 rent aspects of human life in her sound. Shel Khan is a Toronto-based mus
 ician blending alternative\, grunge\, soul\, and industrial music. Her so
 und is fierce\, vulnerable\, and evocative\, with songs exploring themes 
 of ancestry\, nature\, consciousness\, loss\, human connection\, existent
 ialism\, Buddhism\, and dialectics. Human life contains soaring highs\, b
 leak lows\, beauty\, violence\, and everything in between. Shel aspires t
 o touch as much of that multitude as possible. Her debut self-produced EP
 \, Garden\, released May 8\, 2026\, marks a shift toward a darker\, soulf
 ul\, post-industrial alt-rock sound and is only the beginning.
CATEGORIES:Concert,Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Worth-Gallery
