SUMMARY: Solitary Shrew Presents: A fundraiser for Toronto Indigenous Har
 m Reduction featuring Ever Since We Met & Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Each instalment of Solitary Shrew features performances led b
 y women and/or non-binary artists. This month features Ever Since We Met 
 (acoustic emo) and Public Library (punk free jazz) in support of Toronto 
 Indigenous Harm Reduction (TIHR).\n\nFrom TIHR:\n\n"With your donations w
 e will continue to provide our continuous night and bike outreach and hel
 p to purchase and distribute supplies for Indigenous survivors such as cu
 ltural/ ceremonial items and food\, electrolytes and ensure\, harm reduct
 ion kits\, monetary support\, gift cards\, clothing\, sleeping bags\, med
 ical supplies\, socks and other accessories like tarps\, tents\, firewood
 \, and portable lamps. The donations also contribute to emergency travel 
 costs across our traditional territories for Indigenous people in vulnera
 ble situations\, and in cases of bereavement. Your support also provides 
 us with travel and logistical support across the city to continue harm re
 duction and health promotion practices that are desperately needed right 
 now more than ever."\n\nHope to see you there!\n\nP.S. - It's on my birth
 day so you have to come :)
CATEGORIES:Concert,Punk-Rock-Music,emo-music,free-jazz,Tranzac
